  "period_note": "Solo basis. Own contemporaneous annual report: 'Five Years Performance' table (own/current-year column, internally consistent - NII+Net-non-interest-income=operating profit, PBT-tax=PAT, Tier1+Tier2=Total capital all reconcile exactly) plus Note 7.09-7.11 for classified loans and provisioning and the Balance Sheet's off-balance-sheet exposure note. This was the first year the provisioning shortfall stopped being fully offset/plugged by Bangladesh Bank dispensation: required provision (loans+OBS) 27,022,169,469 Taka vs. maintained 10,181,807,044 Taka, a shortfall of 16,840,362,425 Taka (BDT 1,684.04 crore), which the bank's own note states Bangladesh Bank (letter BRPD(P-1)/661/13/2017-2247) allowed to be built up over the following three years (40%/30%/30%) rather than provided for immediately. Classified loans 34,848,500,000 Taka against reported NPL ratio of 20.64% (computed classified/gross-loans = 19.90%, a 0.74pp gap not explained in the source).",
